{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nA file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` has no structural obligation on the implementation. It names no library, algorithm, signature, type, field or named interface that the harness must use or delegate to.\n\nI checked each clause for a behavior-preserving alternative that would violate it:\n- \"MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining the contributions...\", \"include every applicable contribution\" and \"deduplicate identical selections\" describe what the resulting set contains. Any construction that yields the same set, such as a hash set, a sorted merge or a loop, satisfies them. How the set is built is discretionary.\n- \"report unresolvable mandatory inputs before inference\" and \"The complete set MUST be supplied in the initial model request\" constrain observable timing and content. They do not constrain code structure.\n- \"A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and define which sources it contributes and when\" constrains how other requirement texts are written. It does not constrain the harness code.\n- \"A file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`\" and \"A denied selection MUST abort under `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`\" are citations. They point to behavior defined in those requirements. The cited requirements supply context only. `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider` specifies observable scope and gitignore behavior. `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory` specifies abort, reporting, evidence and exit-status behavior.\n\nEvery clause specifies only observable behavior. The review roots are empty, so there are no implementation roots to inspect, and none is needed. Behavioral test adequacy is outside this assessment.\n\nbehavioral: I found no gap. The tests cover each observable obligation of `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`. I did not read any implementation source.\n\n**Combining and including every applicable contribution**\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors]` checks that one bundle holds the subject declaration, cited declarations, terms, and `{impl}`/`{test}` items. It also checks that a distant requirement is excluded.\n- `fn[only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs]` checks that only edges leaving the subject contribute.\n- `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` and `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` check anchor contributions.\n- `fn[references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes]` checks reference contributions, and `fn[generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default]` checks the default omission of generated evidence references.\n- `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` covers citation reviews. `src/authoring/mod.rs` `fn[book_commentary_reviews_supply_the_whole_passage_and_check_concordance]` covers book-commentary reviews. `fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]` covers site reviews.\n\n**Deduplication**\n- `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` cites the same requirement and term repeatedly. It also repeats the built-in `habeas:util` text. It asserts each selection appears once and the total is 5.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs` `fn[behavioral_review_discovers_implementation_locations_without_receiving_their_bodies]` asserts that a recorded input is not duplicated.\n\n**Unresolvable inputs reported before inference**\n- `fn[unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference]` covers a missing file, a missing node, and an ignored file.\n- `fn[disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation]` covers an ignored declaration file.\n- `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` covers an ignored term file.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs` `fn[unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request]` runs the CLI. It asserts a nonzero exit, a stderr message naming the path, that the model endpoint was never contacted, and that evidence was unchanged.\n- `fn[unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment]` checks that stale recorded inputs are not treated as mandatory.\n\n**Complete set in the initial model request**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs` `fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` asserts the first request contains the requirement, the definition, the test item, and the acknowledgment. It also asserts the `prepared_inputs` count equals the initial inputs plus the later reads.\n- `fn[behavioral_review_discovers_implementation_locations_without_receiving_their_bodies]` asserts the first prompt contains the test item and the acknowledgment.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs` `fn[citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations]` asserts the initial request carries the complete mandatory set.\n\n**Visibility under `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`**\n- `fn[mandatory_anchors_respect_git_metadata_and_nested_ignore_exceptions]` covers Git metadata, nested ignore exceptions, an ignored file, and an excepted file.\n- `fn[mandatory_inputs_through_symlinks_leaving_the_project_abort_preparation]` and `fn[outside_test_anchors_stay_outside_the_project_with_an_allow_rule]` cover files outside the project.\n- `fn[evidence_anchors_and_aliases_follow_project_ignore_rules]` covers ignore rules applied through anchors and symlink aliases.\n- `fn[mandatory_inputs_can_read_untracked_declarations_and_terms]` covers untracked files being available.\n\n**Denied selection aborts under `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`**\n- The tests assert `PermissionDenied` errors that name the path and reason, and the CLI test asserts the abort before any model request. The other consequences of that cited requirement belong to its own assessment.\n\nThe duty on contributing requirements to cite this requirement is a drafting obligation on other texts. It is not an observable harness behavior needing a test here.",
